  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lar gibbon protection in Thailands Western Forest Complex</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Lar gibbons are Endangered. The Western Forest Complex (WEFCOM) is one of the last strongholds for this species in Asia. Poaching and habitat loss are major threats to lar gibbon in WEFCOM, and to mitigate this threat WCS-Thailand is working closely with the Government of Thailand to train and equip rangers to protect the lar gibbons of WEFCOM. Lar gibbons are especially sensitive to illegal logging and poaching pressure as they are canopy dwellers, rarely setting foot on the forest floor. Project objectives include: (1) To maintain the SMART (Spatial Monitoring and Reporting Tool) patrol system in Huai Kha Khaeng (HKK) to the current intensity and coverage, and support 22 patrol teams (5 rangers/team) in HKK by providing technical assistance, refresher training, necessary equipment, and patrol ration costs; and (2) To build on previously acquired lar gibbon survey data and establish a baseline population estimate for lar gibbon in the southern area of HKK.</narrative>
  </description>
